The presence of Shigella and other pathogens associated with invasive diarrhea poses significant public health implications. Outbreaks of dysentery can lead to increased healthcare costs, loss of productivity, and strain on healthcare systems. Furthermore, the association of Shigella with obesity suggests that addressing these infections may also have broader health benefits, potentially reducing the prevalence of obesity-related conditions. [Data: Relationships (8136, 17442)]# Muscle Physiology and Strength Training Community

