## Importance of magnesium in muscle function

Muscle tissue serves as a critical site for magnesium, which is vital for various physiological processes, including muscle contraction and energy production. Adequate magnesium levels are necessary for optimal muscle performance, and deficiencies can lead to impaired muscle function and increased risk of injury. This relationship emphasizes the need for proper nutrition to support muscle health and overall physical performance. [Data: Relationships (8321)]

