During stress, muscle tissue releases glutamine, an important amino acid that supports various bodily functions, including immune response and gut health. This release is crucial for athletes, as it helps maintain muscle integrity and supports recovery. Understanding the role of glutamine in muscle physiology can inform training and recovery strategies for athletes. [Data: Relationships (7786)]

