Quilot√≥rax and ascitis quilosa are closely related conditions that involve the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in different body cavities. The management of these conditions often requires similar treatment approaches, emphasizing the importance of understanding their interrelationship. This connection highlights the need for comprehensive care strategies that address both conditions simultaneously, ensuring that patients receive holistic treatment [Data: Entities (11099, 18610); Relationships (18581)].

