The IDDSI standards are integrated into various clinical guidelines and manuals, such as the 'Manual de Disfagia Orofar√≠ngea,' which incorporates IDDSI's framework for effective dysphagia treatment. This integration ensures that healthcare professionals are equipped with the necessary tools and knowledge to manage dysphagia effectively. The manual references specific food texture levels, providing detailed guidelines that align with IDDSI standards, thereby enhancing the quality of care for individuals with swallowing difficulties [Data: Relationships (1148, 1152, 1153, 1154, 1155)].

## Global application of IDDSI guidelines

IDDSI guidelines are applied globally, influencing dysphagia management practices in various countries, including Canada and Chile. These countries utilize IDDSI's standards to define food and liquid textures, ensuring consistency in dietary modifications for individuals with dysphagia. The widespread adoption of IDDSI guidelines underscores their importance in promoting safe eating practices and improving the quality of life for individuals affected by swallowing difficulties [Data: Relationships (4560, 4559)].

