Feeding difficulties (Dificultades en la Alimentaci√≥n) are common among premature newborns, often arising from their physiological immaturity and the availability of maternal milk. These challenges can significantly impact their nutritional intake and overall health. Addressing these difficulties is essential for ensuring that preterm infants receive the necessary nutrition to thrive [Data: Entities (2624); Relationships (10372, +more)].

