The retrospective study highlights that potassium citrate may be associated with a lower prevalence of kidney stones in children on a ketogenic diet. This finding is important as it suggests that while there are concerns regarding growth, there may also be protective benefits against renal complications. Understanding these dual aspects can help in formulating comprehensive dietary guidelines for children undergoing ketogenic treatment. [Data: Entities (11279); Relationships (18682)]# Epilepsy Treatment Community: Epilepsia, MAE, and Dietary Approaches

