Surgical services are integral to the community, providing necessary interventions such as gastrostomy for patients with severe swallowing difficulties. These procedures are critical for ensuring that patients can receive adequate nutrition and manage their health conditions effectively [Data: Reports (2311); Entities (6981); Relationships (3311)]. This highlights the need for collaboration between surgical teams and nutrition specialists to optimize patient care.

