Enteral and parenteral nutrition are vital components of care for many individuals in the PACIENTES community. Patients who cannot meet their nutritional needs through oral intake due to severe malnutrition or medical complications often rely on these forms of nutrition. For example, patients with severe malnutrition may require parenteral nutrition when enteral routes are not feasible, emphasizing the importance of these interventions in their recovery [Data: Reports (2115); Entities (17); Relationships (473, 445)].

