Dysphagia, or difficulty swallowing, is a common issue among patients in the PACIENTES community, particularly those with neurological disorders or after certain surgeries. This condition necessitates specialized care and often requires enteral nutrition to ensure adequate nutrient intake. The Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar√≠ngea plays a critical role in providing tailored interventions for these patients, highlighting the need for specialized services in managing swallowing disorders [Data: Reports (2115); Entities (23); Relationships (423)].

