Regular nutritional assessment and monitoring are essential for patients in the PACIENTES community to identify and address nutritional deficiencies early. Tools such as the NUTRIC SCORE and periodic densitometries are utilized to evaluate the nutritional status and bone health of patients, particularly those receiving parenteral nutrition. This proactive approach is vital for optimizing patient outcomes and preventing complications related to malnutrition [Data: Reports (2115); Entities (561, 500); Relationships (610, 496)].

