Bone mineral density (BMD) is a critical measure for assessing the risk of osteoporosis and fractures in older adults. Regular assessments of BMD can help identify individuals at higher risk and guide interventions to improve bone health. Nutritional factors, including adequate intake of calcium and vitamin D, play a significant role in maintaining bone density. Understanding the relationship between nutrition and BMD is essential for developing effective strategies to prevent osteoporosis in older adults. [Data: Entities (2418, 9922); Relationships (9923)]# Nutritional Emulsions and Parenteral Nutrition Community

