Long-chain triglycerides were used in early formulations of lipid emulsions for parenteral nutrition, providing a source of essential fatty acids. While their use has evolved, they remain an important aspect of nutritional support in medical settings. Understanding the historical context of long-chain triglycerides in lipid emulsions helps to appreciate the advancements in nutritional formulations and their impact on patient care. [Data: Relationships (4726)]

