MEDLINE serves as the central entity in this community, providing a comprehensive bibliographic database of life sciences and biomedical information. It is widely used by researchers and healthcare professionals to access a vast array of literature. The relationships MEDLINE has with other databases, such as EMBASE and Web of Science, highlight its importance in the biomedical literature ecosystem. These connections facilitate a more extensive search capability for users, allowing them to access diverse sources of information that are crucial for systematic reviews and clinical studies. [Data: Entities (16192); Relationships (20482, 20483, 20484)]

