The relationships between MEDLINE and other databases like EMBASE and Web of Science illustrate a collaborative network that enhances the accessibility of biomedical literature. For instance, both MEDLINE and EMBASE index biomedical literature, which allows researchers to cross-reference and validate findings across multiple platforms. This interconnectivity is vital for comprehensive literature reviews and ensures that researchers have access to a wide range of studies and articles, thereby improving the quality of their research outcomes. [Data: Relationships (20482, 20483)]

