## Complications arising from catheter insertion

The insertion of central venous catheters can lead to various complications, including pneumothorax, hemothorax, and gas embolism. These complications can significantly impact patient outcomes and highlight the importance of skilled personnel during catheter placement. Understanding these risks is essential for healthcare providers to minimize adverse events. [Data: Entities (2059, 2060, 14876); Relationships (8764, 8766, 19179)]

