VED and VFS are pivotal diagnostic tools in the evaluation of swallowing disorders. VED focuses on the pharyngeal phase of swallowing, while VFS provides a comprehensive analysis of the oral phase. Both tests are essential for healthcare professionals to accurately diagnose and treat patients with dysphagia. Their complementary nature enhances the overall assessment process, allowing for a thorough understanding of the patient's swallowing capabilities. [Data: Entities (392, 391); Relationships (3007)]

