## Understanding Hipercalcemia Hipocalci√∫rica Familiar (HHF)

Hipercalcemia hipocalci√∫rica familiar (HHF) is an autosomal dominant hereditary disorder that significantly affects calcium regulation in the body. This condition arises from mutations in the CASR gene, which plays a crucial role in calcium homeostasis. The implications of HHF are profound, as it can lead to elevated calcium levels in the blood, which may cause various health issues. Understanding HHF is essential for identifying at-risk individuals and providing appropriate medical care. [Data: Entities (5632, 5634); Relationships (15094)]

