Paratiroidectom√≠a, or parathyroid surgery, is indicated for certain patients with HHF, particularly those with mild primary hyperparathyroidism. This surgical intervention can help manage calcium levels and alleviate symptoms associated with hypercalcemia. The relationship between HHF and paratiroidectom√≠a emphasizes the need for tailored treatment plans based on individual patient profiles and the severity of their condition. [Data: Entities (5633); Relationships (15093)]

