Lactobacillus strains, such as Lactobacillus gasseri and Lactobacillus rhamnosus, have demonstrated beneficial effects on obesity and metabolic health. These strains are part of the microbiota that can positively influence weight management and metabolic functions. Their inclusion in dietary interventions may offer a promising approach to obesity treatment and prevention [Data: Entities (9065, 9064); Relationships (17395, 17394, +more)].# Akkermansia Muciniphila and Metabolic Health Community

