Chemotherapy is often used as a preparatory treatment before hematopoietic cell transplantation to eliminate cancerous cells. However, it can also lead to complications that affect recovery and overall health. The timing and type of chemotherapy administered can significantly influence the success of the transplant and the patient's subsequent health status. Therefore, careful planning and management of chemotherapy regimens are essential to improve transplant outcomes. [Data: Entities (13741, 13786); Relationships (897, 881)]# Diabetes Management and Complications Community

