Gastrostom√≠a Endosc√≥pica Percut√°nea (PEG) is a procedure designed for patients requiring long-term enteral nutrition. This method allows for the placement of a feeding tube directly into the stomach, making it suitable for patients who need nutritional support for more than 4-6 weeks. The procedure is particularly beneficial for patients with chronic conditions that impair their ability to eat normally. However, it is associated with risks such as wound infection and complications like buried bumper syndrome. [Data: Entities (1872); Relationships (3186, 619, 731, 7728, 7729, +more)]

