Hypoxaluria primaria is a genetic disorder that leads to abnormal oxalate levels in the body, affecting kidney function. This condition can manifest in two forms: one leading to hyperoxaluria and the other to hypoxaluria. The genetic basis of this disorder emphasizes the importance of genetic counseling and testing for affected individuals and their families. Understanding the hereditary nature of hypoxaluria primaria can aid in early diagnosis and management, potentially reducing the risk of kidney stone formation. [Data: Entities (11952); Relationships (18924)]

