## Significance of dietary modifications for dysphagia patients

Dietoterapia addresses the dietary needs of patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. The identification of dangerous foods, such as sticky items and those that can easily fragment, is crucial for ensuring the safety of these patients. Caregivers and healthcare providers must be aware of these hazardous foods to prevent choking or aspiration. The relationship between diet therapy and dysphagia management highlights the importance of tailored dietary interventions in clinical settings. [Data: Entities (1224); Relationships (464, 386)]

