## Adrenoleukodystrophy as a central disorder

Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD) is a genetic disorder that significantly impacts lipid metabolism, leading to severe neurological and adrenal complications. The disorder is characterized by the accumulation of very long-chain fatty acids, which can result in a range of symptoms including neuropathy, cardiac arrhythmias, and adrenal insufficiency. The progressive nature of ALD necessitates careful management and treatment to mitigate its effects on patients' health. [Data: Entities (11052); Relationships (8871, 14959, 18556, 18558, 18564)]

